{
  "format": "cam_gradr-layout/2",
  "notes": [
    "Geometry and order only, derived from photos of an SCK300. No color values, no manufacturer designations.",
    "Two color cards in portrait orientation, 4 columns x 6 rows each. Card 1 = columns A-D, card 2 = columns E-H; letter = column, digit = row from the top.",
    "Rectangles are relative to the black card plate (0..1, origin top left): the dark area the app detects, without the light case around it and without the gray shadow of the case wall next to it.",
    "role \"neutral\": fields of the two gray ramps (columns D and E); they provide the white balance and the tone curve.",
    "Measured on 4 stills of each card pair (two webcams, 1280 x 720, cards at about 35-80 % of the image height, some held rotated by 180 degrees): corners from the detection at full resolution, then the four edges of every field where the color passes the middle between the black plate and the field, and one regular grid fitted through them. The spread between the shots is about 0.5 % of the card size; checked by leaving each shot out of the fit. Both color cards share the same grid."
  ],
